<title>GERMANY: German inland off in quiet trade before holiday.</title>
<headline>German inland off in quiet trade before holiday.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.6900)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     34.20/34.40     20.19/20.31   34.50/34.80</p>
<p> BREMEN		34.20/34.40     20.19/20.31   34.50/34.80</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    34.20/34.40     20.19/20.31   34.50/34.80</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   34.80/34.90     20.55/20.61   35.10/35.20</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   34.90/35.00     20.61/20.67   35.10/35.20</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  35.90/36.10     21.20/21.32   36.30/36.40</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices eased further on Wednesday as they played catch-up with Tuesday's gas oil futures losses and many markets went dead ahead of the Corpus Christi public holiday in parts of Germany -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714.</p>
